              "inlines": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "In-scope variables"
                }
              ],
              "rowspan": 1,
              "style": null,
              "valign": "top"
            }
          ]
        ],
        "id": null,
        "options": [],
        "roles": [],
        "stripes": null,
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Antora extension events and in-scope variables"
          }
        ],
        "width": 100
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The playbook object (i.e., the parsed data from the playbook file) is available at the time the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "register"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " function is called (which acts like the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "register"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event). However, at this stage, the playbook is still just a raw data model. The Antora extensions have yet to be registered. When the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "contextStarted"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is emitted, all the initialization of the playbook, including registering Antora extensions and generator functions, is complete."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When modifying the content sources in an Antora extension, it’s customary to use the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "playbookBuilt"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event. After that, the playbook object cannot be modified or updated."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Antora creates the component version objects from the component version buckets in the content aggregate. Then Antora emits the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "componentsRegistered"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event. At that point, additional files can be added to "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "files"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " property on a given component version object. After the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "componentsRegistered"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event, Antora adds the files attached to each component version to the content catalog. After the files are added for each component version, Antora registers the component version start page. Once the files are added for all component versions, Antora registers the site start page."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Once Antora has published the site, it provides the locations of all output destinations (also called "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "publications"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "emphasis",
            "roles": [
              "term"
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ") in the form of an array of objects via the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "publications"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " variable passed to (and only to) the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "sitePublished"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In addition to the built-in context variables listed in this table, your extension can also access context variables documented and promoted by other extensions."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "id": "register",
        "index": "1",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The register function isn’t an event, but rather the function Antora calls on an extension so it can register listeners."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "functions",
        "index": "2",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The built-in generator functions are not available until this event is emitted."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "event-sequence",
        "index": "3",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "uiLoaded"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event may be emitted before, between, or after the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "contentAggregated"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "componentsRegistered"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " events."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": null,
        "index": "4",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The contentCatalog only provides access to the component versions at this phase, which are still in the process of being constructed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": null,
        "index": "5",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "siteMapped"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event is only emitted if the site URL is specified in the playbook."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": null,
        "index": "6",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Listeners of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "contextClosed"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " event are expected to catch their own errors so all listeners are notified."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Generator Lifecycle Events Reference"
      }
    ]
  }
